questions.question:
The Delivered button now checks NetInfo first. A courier in the basement car park of a Thu Duc apartment block still sees an error:

```ts
const state = await NetInfo.fetch();
if (state.isConnected) {
  await api.post(`/deliveries/${id}/complete`);
}
```

```text
NetInfo: { type: "wifi", isConnected: true, isInternetReachable: false }
[api] POST /deliveries/d-8812/complete
TypeError: Network request failed
```

Statement: "If NetInfo reports `isConnected: true`, the request will reach the server, so checking it before every write prevents these failures."

The delivery list screen today:

```tsx
const [deliveries, setDeliveries] = useState<Delivery[] | null>(null);
useEffect(() => {
  api.get("/couriers/me/deliveries").then(setDeliveries);
}, []);
if (!deliveries) return <Spinner />;
```

Statement: "Reading the list from the phone's database first and refreshing it in the background shows the last known deliveries at once in a basement, at the cost of data that may be stale, which the screen should label (for example 'updated 4 min ago')."
